# Tests via peaky-test

Python tests for `peaky_finders` run **inside the `peaky:dev` Docker image**, not on the macOS host.

## Do this

- Run tests with **`./peaky-test`** from the repo root (same image/build knobs as `./peaky` web server: `--build`, `PEAKY_DEV_IMAGE`, `PEAKY_CACHE_DIR`).
- Pass pytest args through: `./peaky-test tests/test_mesh_connectivity.py`, `./peaky-test -k foo`, `./peaky-test --build`.
- When verifying changes, use `./peaky-test` (or a targeted path) instead of `poetry run pytest` on the host.

## Avoid

- **`poetry install` / `poetry run pytest` on the host** in `peaky_finders/` — it creates or corrupts the bind-mounted `.venv` (Linux vs macOS interpreters and wheels).
- Assuming `pytest` on PATH is the correct test environment; splatter/GDAL deps live in the container.

## Why

`./peaky` runs the web server in Docker with `peaky_finders/` bind-mounted. The in-project `.venv` must stay **Linux-only**. `./peaky-test` keeps test runs on the same contract.
